# Dotfiles

## Add User (as root)

```bash
USERNAME=myuser &&
useradd -m -s /bin/bash "$USERNAME" &&
usermod -aG sudo "$USERNAME" &&
passwd "$USERNAME" &&
[ -f /root/.ssh/authorized_keys ] && {
    cp -r /root/.ssh "/home/$USERNAME/" &&
    chown -R "$USERNAME:$USERNAME" "/home/$USERNAME/.ssh" &&
    chmod 700 "/home/$USERNAME/.ssh" &&
    chmod 600 "/home/$USERNAME/.ssh/"*
}
```

## Install Dotfiles (as user)

```bash
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexander-bech/dotfiles/master/.local/bin/install-dotfiles.sh | bash
```

Use `--https` if SSH isn't configured, `--no-extras` to skip optional software.
